<title>UK: Higher prices sidelined UK meals and feeds buyers.</title>
<headline>Higher prices sidelined UK meals and feeds buyers.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Firm high protein soymeal on Friday kept most buyers on the sidelines of the UK meals and feeds market.</p>
<p>High pro sellers pushed up prices by as much as three stg a tonne following a surge in Chicago futures on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;Most people are in no hurry to buy and prices like this will only keep them out of the market longer,&quot; said one broker.</p>
<p>--Jim Ballantyne, London Newsroom, +44 171 542 8062</p>
